WEBVTT

00:00.690 --> 00:03.770
The measure of two angles
of an isosceles triangle

00:03.770 --> 00:09.340
are 3x plus 5 degrees, we'll
say, and x plus 16 degrees.

00:09.340 --> 00:11.630
Find all possible values of x.

00:11.630 --> 00:12.740
So let's think about this.

00:12.740 --> 00:16.420
Let's draw ourselves an
isosceles triangle or two.

00:16.420 --> 00:21.301
So it's an isosceles triangle,
like that and like that.

00:21.301 --> 00:23.050
And actually, let me
draw a couple of them

00:23.050 --> 00:24.290
just because we want
to think about all

00:24.290 --> 00:25.920
of the different
possibilities here.

00:29.400 --> 00:32.202
So we know, from what we know
about isosceles triangles,

00:32.202 --> 00:34.160
that the base angles are
going to be congruent.

00:34.160 --> 00:36.360
So that angle is going to
be equal to that angle.

00:36.360 --> 00:38.620
That angle is going to
be equal to that angle.

00:38.620 --> 00:42.490
And so what could the 3x plus
5 degrees and the x plus 16,

00:42.490 --> 00:43.980
what could they be measures of?

00:43.980 --> 00:45.690
Well, maybe this
one right over here

00:45.690 --> 00:48.980
has a measure of
3x plus 5 degrees.

00:48.980 --> 00:51.090
And the vertex is the other one.

00:51.090 --> 00:56.570
So maybe this one up here
is the x plus 16 degrees.

00:56.570 --> 00:59.530
The other possibility
is that this

00:59.530 --> 01:02.000
is describing both base
angles, in which case,

01:02.000 --> 01:03.380
they would be equal.

01:03.380 --> 01:07.540
So maybe this one is 3x plus
5, and maybe this one over here

01:07.540 --> 01:08.745
is x plus 16.

01:11.480 --> 01:13.520
And then the final
possibility-- actually we

01:13.520 --> 01:15.150
haven't exhausted
all of them-- is

01:15.150 --> 01:18.080
if we swap these two--
if this one is x plus 16,

01:18.080 --> 01:19.730
and that one is 3x plus 5.

01:19.730 --> 01:21.760
So let me draw ourselves
another triangle.

01:25.630 --> 01:27.440
And obviously swapping
these two aren't

01:27.440 --> 01:29.430
going to make a
difference because they

01:29.430 --> 01:30.825
are equal to each other.

01:30.825 --> 01:32.950
And then we could make that
one equal to 3x plus 5.

01:32.950 --> 01:34.480
But that's not going to
change anything either

01:34.480 --> 01:35.980
because they're
equal to each other.

01:35.980 --> 01:40.160
So the last situation is
where this angle down here

01:40.160 --> 01:47.990
is x plus 16, and this
angle up here is 3x plus 5.

01:47.990 --> 01:49.650
This is 3x plus 5.

01:49.650 --> 01:51.960
So let's just work
through each of these.

01:51.960 --> 01:55.220
So in this situation, if
this base angle is 3x plus 5,

01:55.220 --> 01:57.100
so is this base angle.

01:57.100 --> 01:58.860
And then we know that
all three of these

01:58.860 --> 02:00.730
are going to have to
add up to 180 degrees.

02:00.730 --> 02:05.920
So we get 3x plus
5 plus 3x plus 5

02:05.920 --> 02:14.260
plus x plus 16 is going to
be equal to 180 degrees.

02:14.260 --> 02:15.420
We have 3x.

02:15.420 --> 02:16.370
Let's just add up.

02:16.370 --> 02:19.140
You have 3x plus
3x, which gives you

02:19.140 --> 02:23.880
6x, plus another x gives you 7x.

02:23.880 --> 02:27.950
And then you have 5
plus 5, which is 10,

02:27.950 --> 02:29.600
plus 16 is equal to 26.

02:32.600 --> 02:36.030
And that is going
to be equal to 180.

02:36.030 --> 02:39.070
And then we have, let's
see, 180 minus 26.

02:39.070 --> 02:45.210
If we subtract 26 from both
sides, we get 180 minus 20

02:45.210 --> 02:52.790
is 160, minus another 6 is 154.

02:52.790 --> 02:57.460
You have 7x is equal to 154.

02:57.460 --> 03:01.408
And let's see how many times--
if we divide both sides by 7,

03:01.408 --> 03:06.800
7 will go into 140 20 times,
and then you have another 14.

03:06.800 --> 03:08.235
So it looks like it's 22 times.

03:08.235 --> 03:10.140
So x is equal to 22.

03:10.140 --> 03:10.990
Is that right?

03:10.990 --> 03:13.930
20 times 7 is 140.

03:13.930 --> 03:18.210
140 plus 14 is 154.

03:18.210 --> 03:24.700
So we have x is equal
to 22 degrees in this

03:24.700 --> 03:26.140
the first scenario.

03:26.140 --> 03:29.200
Now let's think about the
second scenario over here.

03:29.200 --> 03:32.080
Now we have these
two characters are

03:32.080 --> 03:34.070
going to be equal to each
other because they're

03:34.070 --> 03:35.500
both the base angles.

03:35.500 --> 03:41.100
So you have 3x plus 5
is equal to x plus 16.

03:41.100 --> 03:43.340
Well, you can subtract
x from both sides.

03:43.340 --> 03:48.450
And so this becomes 2x
plus 5 is equal to 16.

03:48.450 --> 03:51.070
We can subtract
5 from both sides

03:51.070 --> 03:54.510
and you get 2x is equal to 11.

03:54.510 --> 03:58.190
And then you can
divide both sides by 2,

03:58.190 --> 04:03.330
and you get x is equal to 11/2.

04:03.330 --> 04:05.830
So that is our second scenario.

04:05.830 --> 04:08.270
And then we do our third
scenario right over here.

04:08.270 --> 04:12.370
If this base angle is x plus
16, then this base angle

04:12.370 --> 04:14.850
right over here is also
going to be x plus 16.

04:14.850 --> 04:15.954
They are congruent.

04:15.954 --> 04:17.329
And then we can
do the same thing

04:17.329 --> 04:19.420
that we did for
the first scenario.

04:19.420 --> 04:22.670
All of these angles are going to
have to add up to 180 degrees.

04:22.670 --> 04:28.665
So we have x plus 16 plus
x plus 16 plus 3x plus 5.

04:31.437 --> 04:33.020
When you add them
all together, you're

04:33.020 --> 04:36.570
going to get 180 degrees.

04:36.570 --> 04:38.020
Now let's add up
all the x terms.

04:38.020 --> 04:42.880
x plus x is 2x plus 3x is 5x.

04:42.880 --> 04:46.160
So we get 5x.

04:46.160 --> 04:50.550
And then you have
16 plus 16 is 32.

04:50.550 --> 04:52.800
32 plus 5 is 37.

04:52.800 --> 04:56.055
Plus 37 is equal to 180 degrees.

04:59.350 --> 05:01.710
Subtract 37 from
both sides, and we

05:01.710 --> 05:08.180
get 5x is equal to
180 minus 30 is 150.

05:08.180 --> 05:09.850
So that gets us to 143.

05:09.850 --> 05:11.620
So it's not going
to divide nicely.

05:11.620 --> 05:16.260
Divide both sides by 5,
you get x is equal 143/5,

05:16.260 --> 05:18.260
which we can just leave
as an improper fraction.

05:18.260 --> 05:19.440
You could write it
as a mixed number

05:19.440 --> 05:21.530
or however else you
might want to write it.

05:21.530 --> 05:22.460
And we're done.

05:22.460 --> 05:29.470
These are the three
possible values

05:29.470 --> 05:33.730
of x, given the information that
they gave us right up there.
